- `age == "16"` :: `"16"` in quotes is a string, and a string is never equal to a number. This is `False`.
- `not age < 18` :: `age < 18` is `True` (16 is less than 18), and `not` flips it to `False`.
* `age < 10 or age != 15` :: Right. `age < 10` is `False`, but `age != 15` is `True` (16 isn't 15). `or` needs only one `True` side.
