hint: Watch out for `>` versus `>=`, quotes around a number, and `not`, which flips the answer after the comparison.
hint: Three of the six are `True`.
right: The three `True` ones: `16 >= 16` (equal counts for `>=`), `13 <= 16 <= 19` (both pairs hold), and `False or True` (one `True` side is enough for `or`).
wrong: Put 16 in place of `age` and work out each one. `>` doesn't include equal. `"16"` is text, so it's never equal to the number 16. `not` flips the result of the comparison after it. `or` is `True` if either side is `True`.

