hint: `is_valid = long_enough and no_spaces and ends_with_digit`
right: `len("sun day7")` is 8, so `long_enough` is `True`. There is a space, so `no_spaces` is `False`. The last character is `"7"`, so `ends_with_digit` is `True`. `True and False and True` is `False`, so this password is rejected. Change it to `"sunday77"` and all four become `True`.
wrong: Build each boolean with a comparison: `len(password) >= 8`, `" " not in password` and `password[-1].isdigit()`. Then `is_valid` joins all three with `and`, so a single failed rule makes it `False`.

